<article class="env-lemma" id="07Z7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07Z7">Lemma <span data-tag="07Z7">15.8.1</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $A$ be an $n \times m$ matrix with coefficients in $R$. Let $I_ r(A)$ be the ideal generated by the $r \times r$-minors of $A$ with the convention that $I_0(A) = R$ and $I_ r(A) = 0$ if $r > \min (n, m)$. Then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$I_0(A) \supset I_1(A) \supset I_2(A) \supset \ldots $, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
if $B$ is an $(n + n') \times m$ matrix, and $A$ is the first $n$ rows of $B$, then $I_{r + n'}(B) \subset I_ r(A)$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
if $C$ is an $n \times n$ matrix then $I_ r(CA) \subset I_ r(A)$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $A$ is a block matrix 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \left( \begin{matrix}  A_1 

&  0 

\\  0 

&  A_2 

\end{matrix} \right)  \]
</div>
<p>
 then $I_ r(A) = \sum _{r_1 + r_2 = r} I_{r_1}(A_1) I_{r_2}(A_2)$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Add more here. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
